<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-08-11T17:30:37+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Tue, 11 Aug 2026 17:30:37 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Atlanta turned a 7,000-pound Colorado turbine blade into a 50-foot bridge at Beaverbrook Park]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133153113.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a remarkable display of innovation, a retired wind turbine blade has been repurposed into a pedestrian bridge at Beaverbrook Park in Atlanta. This 15-meter structure, weighing around 7,000 pounds, was transported from Colorado and creatively adapted by researchers to fulfill the role of public infrastructure. This pioneering project marks the first instance of its kind in the United States, building upon the Re-Wind Network's prior endeavors.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/atlanta-reused-a-nearly-7000-pound-wind-turbine-blade-as-a-50-foot-pedestrian-bridge-the-retired-colorado-blade-now-carries-walkers-through-beaverbrook-park/articleshow/133153113.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/atlanta-reused-a-nearly-7000-pound-wind-turbine-blade-as-a-50-foot-pedestrian-bridge-the-retired-colorado-blade-now-carries-walkers-through-beaverbrook-park/articleshow/133153113.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-11T17:21:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133153319,imgsize-178196.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Why is Chud The Builder finally out of jail after two months? Here’s what we know]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133147934.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Dalton Eatherly, known as Chud The Builder, has been released from jail after two months. He posted a $1 million bond, securing his freedom from Montgomery County Jail. Eatherly faces attempted murder charges linked to a May courthouse shooting incident. He is also involved in a separate Davidson County case for alleged restaurant theft. Both cases are now proceeding to a grand jury for further review.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/why-is-chud-the-builder-finally-out-of-jail-after-two-months-heres-what-we-know/articleshow/133147934.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/why-is-chud-the-builder-finally-out-of-jail-after-two-months-heres-what-we-know/articleshow/133147934.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-11T16:05:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Global Sports Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133148036,imgsize-453085.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[California woman refused to sell her home; developers built a 246-unit complex around it]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133152851.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/california-woman-refused-to-sell-her-home-despite-repeated-lucrative-offers-developers-eventually-built-a-246-unit-apartment-complex-around-her-house-covering-five-acres/articleshow/133152851.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/california-woman-refused-to-sell-her-home-despite-repeated-lucrative-offers-developers-eventually-built-a-246-unit-apartment-complex-around-her-house-covering-five-acres/articleshow/133152851.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-11T17:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133153322,imgsize-1440733.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Dennis Hope: The man who claimed the Moon and made millions]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133150695.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/meet-dennis-hope-the-unemployed-man-who-claimed-the-moon-sold-611-million-acres-and-made-millions-from-19-95-lunar-plots/articleshow/133150695.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/meet-dennis-hope-the-unemployed-man-who-claimed-the-moon-sold-611-million-acres-and-made-millions-from-19-95-lunar-plots/articleshow/133150695.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-11T17:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133152963,imgsize-50943.cms"/></item><item><ti