33151259,imgsize-1186327.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[UK Muslim charity under terror probe over alleged Hamas ties after senior figure arrested in US case]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133152968.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/uk-muslim-charity-under-terror-probe-over-alleged-hamas-ties-after-senior-figure-arrested-in-us-case/articleshow/133152968.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/uk-muslim-charity-under-terror-probe-over-alleged-hamas-ties-after-senior-figure-arrested-in-us-case/articleshow/133152968.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-11T17:13:16+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133153180,imgsize-164854.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A buried river was uncovered in Yonkers; 6 months later, wildlife had a 14,000 sq ft habitat]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133147516.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In 2012, Yonkers, New York, completed a project to uncover a section of the Saw Mill River that had been buried beneath a downtown parking lot since the 1920s. The former Larkin Plaza was turned into a three-acre public park. Within six months, the restored river supported 14,000 square feet of new aquatic habitat and several species.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2012-yonkers-tore-up-a-downtown-parking-lot-to-uncover-a-river-buried-for-decades-within-six-months-it-had-created-14000-sq-ft-of-aquatic-habitat/articleshow/133147516.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2012-yonkers-tore-up-a-downtown-parking-lot-to-uncover-a-river-buried-for-decades-within-six-months-it-had-created-14000-sq-ft-of-aquatic-habitat/articleshow/133147516.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-11T15:09:31+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133149436,imgsize-152626.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ireland brought white-tailed eagles back after more than a century: 245 chicks released, breeding continues in 2026]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133152582.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Once extinct, white-tailed eagles now soar across Ireland's skies again. Conservationists released 245 young eagles since 2007, which has boosted the population. These magnificent birds are now breeding and expanding their territory independently across the country. The National Parks and Wildlife Service estimates around 150 eagles live in the wild. Despite ongoing threats, the species is successfully recovering and raising its young.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/irelands-white-tailed-eagles-went-extinct-due-to-human-persecution-now-the-country-has-released-245-chicks-in-the-wild-about-100-years-later/articleshow/133152582.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/irelands-white-tailed-eagles-went-extinct-due-to-human-persecution-now-the-country-has-released-245-chicks-in-the-wild-about-100-years-later/articleshow/133152582.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-11T16:58:57+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133152810,imgsize-56838.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1942, Crazy Horse’s sacred bundle was buried in Nebraska; decades later, it vanished]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133151050.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Fast Thunder was given Crazy Horse's sacred medicine bundle before 1877, which then became a closely guarded family heirloom for many years. In 1942, Theodore Means buried this bundle in Minatare, Nebraska, but due to significant landscape alterations in the area, its burial site has remained undiscoverable. The details of the bundle's contents and its precise location continue to be a puzzling enigma.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1942-crazy-horses-sacred-medicine-bundle-was-buried-underground-in-nebraska-decades-later-the-family-returned-to-find-its-landmark-gone/articleshow/133151050.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1942-crazy-horses-sacred-medicine-bundle-was-buried-underground-in-nebraska-decades-later-the-family-returned-to-find-its-landmark-gone/articleshow/133151050.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-11T16:08:59+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133151326,imgsize-183687.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Two Pakistanis, one Indonesian killed in Houthi attack on cargo ship in Bab el-Mandeb]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133151038.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/two-pakistanis-one-indonesian-killed-in-houthi-attack-on-cargo-ship-in-bab-el-mandeb/articleshow/133151038.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/two-pakistanis-one-indonesian-killed-in-houthi-attack-on-cargo-ship-in-bab-el-mandeb/articleshow/133151038.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-11T16:29:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133152043,imgsize-314890.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[New Haven landfill turned into solar farm now powers about 200 homes and pays the city $72,000 a year]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133149344.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[New Haven is transforming a decommissioned landfill into a major solar energy project, installation of 1,920 solar panels that will produce a significant amount of clean energy every year. With anticipated revenue exceeding $1.4 million over two decades, this venture supports New Haven's dedication to enhancing its renewable energy initiatives, ultimately benefitting both the environment and the local economy.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/new-haven-turned-a-capped-landfill-into-a-1920-panel-solar-farm-the-site-now-powers-about-200-homes-and-pays-the-city-72000-a-year/articleshow/133149344.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/new-haven-turned-a-capped-landfill-into-a-1920-panel-solar-farm-the-site-now-powers-about-200-homes-and-pays-the-city-72000-a-year/articleshow/133149344.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-11T15:06:19+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133149443,imgsize-166154.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Montreal man, 51, charged with death threats against Canadian PM Mark Carney]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133150995.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/montreal-man-51-charged-with-death-threats-against-canadian-pm-mark-carney/articleshow/133150995.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/montreal-man-51-charged-with-death-threats-against-canadian-pm-mark-carney/articleshow/133150995.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-11T16:25:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aashish Vashistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133151551,imgsize-67227.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[California built beaver-like dams in coho creeks; survival rose from 8% to 60% after restoration]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133149367.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Innovative restoration initiatives that emulate beaver dams have drastically enhanced coho salmon survival rates, boosting juvenile survival in a specific creek from eight percent to sixty percent. By generating cooler, slower water environments, these structures are essential for nurturing young salmon. Furthermore, these revitalized areas bolster resistance to drought conditions within the Scott River watershed, underscoring the necessity of reinstating vital wetland habitats for at-risk salmon species.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/california-built-beaver-like-dams-in-coho-salmon-creeks-at-one-site-mean-juvenile-survival-rose-from-8-before-restoration-to-60-after/articleshow/133149367.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/california-built-beaver-like-dams-in-coho-salmon-creeks-at-one-site-mean-juvenile-survival-rose-from-8-before-restoration-to-60-after/articleshow/133149367.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-11T15:07:59+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133149491,imgsize-1327248.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Congo’s Ebola death toll crosses 2,000 as country battles fastest-growing outbreak]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133149607.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/congos-ebola-death-toll-crosses-2000-as-country-battles-fastest-growing-outbreak/articleshow/133149607.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/congos-ebola-death-toll-crosses-2000-as-country-battles-fastest-growing-outbreak/articleshow/133149607.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-11T15:21:01+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133149745,imgsize-104548.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[QTCinderella’s homophobic friends controversy explained: Streamer under fire over past comments]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133149275.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[QTCinderella has responded after renewed criticism over claims that she associates with “homophobic people.” The streamer explained that she believes kindness and personal relationships can help people reconsider harmful beliefs. She also admitted that her comments from a year ago were poorly worded and said she is not friends with bigots. After more confusion online, she shared a longer explanation on her main X account.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/qtcinderellas-homophobic-friends-controversy-explained-streamer-addresses-backlash-over-her-past-comments/articleshow/133149275.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-st